  "description": "WESSIZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C57 H70 Eu4 N12 O23,2(C1 H4 O1),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.911-3.967 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.79-111.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu4L4(CO3)(acac)2(H2O)2(CH3OH)2]·5H2O·2CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
